# .npmignore — overrides `files` in package.json for matching paths.
# We use `files` as the include list and this as the targeted-exclude
# layer so test sources and dev-only directories don't ship.
#
# Anchored exclusions for the three known test files. Glob patterns
# (*.test.ts, **/*.test.ts) silently fail to match nested files under
# the npm pack semantics that interact with `files` allowlists.
src/cli/commands/skill/install-cmd.test.ts
src/cli/commands/skill/validate.test.ts
src/cli/parse-platforms.test.ts

# NOTE: the dev-only `gui/README.md` is NOT excluded here — npm force-includes
# README* files regardless of .npmignore (verified: /gui/README.md, gui/*.md,
# README.md patterns all fail to suppress it). It is removed at `prepack`
# instead (scripts/gui-pack-prune.ts) and restored by `postpack`.

tests
docs
.claude
.yolo-sisyphus
